  {
    "bundleBaseUrl": "",
    "bundleFileTemplate": "/datasets/mouse_pomc_maternal_hfd_gse135639/track_{trackId}.js",
    "category": "Developmental programming",
    "citation": "Offspring arcuate POMC-neuron translatome (RiboTag), maternal chow vs high-fat diet at P0 and P21 — the 2×2 design browsable as four contrasts: the maternal-diet effect at each age separately (exploratory; not contrasts the source study ran) and the study's own P0→P21 maturation axis per diet arm. Gestational malprogramming; Haddad-Tóvolli et al., Mol Metab 2020 (GSE135639, PMID 32283518)",
    "contrasts": [
      {
        "baseline": "chow_p0",
        "case": "hfd_p0",
        "description": "Exploratory simple effect from the 2×2, not a contrast from the source paper: maternal HFD vs chow among newborn (P0) offspring only, 5 vs 5 libraries. Fitted as a cell-means contrast with the residual variance pooled across all 17 libraries (limma-trend).",
        "exploratory": true,
        "group": "Maternal-diet effect",
        "id": "hfd_vs_chow_p0",
        "label": "Maternal HFD vs chow · at P0",
      },
      {
        "baseline": "chow_p21",
        "case": "hfd_p21",
        "description": "Exploratory simple effect from the 2×2, not a contrast from the source paper: maternal HFD vs chow among weaning-age (P21) offspring only, 3 vs 4 libraries. Fitted as a cell-means contrast with the residual variance pooled across all 17 libraries (limma-trend).",
        "exploratory": true,
        "group": "Maternal-diet effect",
        "id": "hfd_vs_chow_p21",
        "isDefault": true,
        "label": "Maternal HFD vs chow · at P21",
      },
      {
        "baseline": "chow_p0",
        "case": "chow_p21",
        "description": "The source study's own axis: the P0→P21 maturation trajectory within the maternal-chow arm (3 vs 5 libraries), re-fit here with limma-trend on the deposited CPM rather than the paper's pipeline. Compare against the HFD arm's trajectory — the paper's finding is that maternal HFD enlarges it.",
        "group": "Maturation (P0 → P21)",
        "id": "p21_vs_p0_chow",
        "label": "P21 vs P0 · chow arm (maturation)",
      },
      {
        "baseline": "hfd_p0",
        "case": "hfd_p21",
        "description": "The source study's own axis: the P0→P21 maturation trajectory within the maternal-HFD arm (4 vs 5 libraries), re-fit here with limma-trend on the deposited CPM rather than the paper's pipeline. More genes move here than in the chow arm, the direction the paper reports as gestational malprogramming.",
        "group": "Maturation (P0 → P21)",
        "id": "p21_vs_p0_hfd",
        "label": "P21 vs P0 · HFD arm (maturation)",
      },
    ],
